# Kenwood TS-890S PC CONTROL COMMAND REFERENCE GUIDE
# Printed revision/date: no revision printed; cover date "January/30/2019".
# Command: FV "Firmware Version"
# Printed page 34 = PDF page 35. Charts used: Read, Answer. (No Set chart is printed.)
# Derivation date: 08/09/2026.
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS
#   Read   : 3 positions. Ruler 1..10; cells 'F' 'V' ';'. Terminator at printed position 3.
#   Answer : 7 positions. Ruler 1..10; cells 'F' 'V' P1 P1 P1 P1 ';'. Terminator at printed
#            position 7. Every header is a NUMBER.
#
# POSITION MAP
#   Read    1 'F'   2 'V'   3 ';'
#   Answer  1 'F'   2 'V'   3-6 P1 (four positions)   7 ';'
#
# LEGEND, VERBATIM
#   "P1"
#   "  Character string of the firmware version."
#   worked example, VERBATIM:
#   "For example: "FV1.00;" (firmware version 1.00)"
#
#   The worked example is 7 characters and lands exactly on the counted chart: F V 1 . 0 0 ;
#   so P1 = "1.00" occupies positions 3,4,5,6 and the '.' is a real frame byte.
#
# INHERITED-ASSUMED bytes: none. The Answer vector below is the book's own printed example.
#   The book does not say what happens if a version string is not four characters long; the
#   chart gives P1 exactly four positions.
#
# VECTORS
read	FV;
answer_printed_example	FV1.00;
